mastery.question_text:
A semicircle has the same area as a square of side $10$ cm.
Find the radius of the semicircle, correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\draw[thick] (0,0) rectangle (2,2);
\node[below] at (1,0) {$10\text{ cm}$};
\draw[thick] (4,0) -- (7.2,0);
\draw[thick] (7.2,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=180,radius=1.6];
\fill (5.6,0) circle (1.5pt);
\draw[dashed] (5.6,0) -- (6.518,1.311) node[midway,above left] {$r$};
\node at (3.6,-0.65) {equal areas};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A circular pond of area $50$ m$^{2}$ sits at the centre of a circular lawn.
Pond and lawn together cover $120$ m$^{2}$.
Find the width $w$ of the ring of lawn, correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\draw[thick] (0,0) circle (2.4);
\draw[thick] (0,0) circle (1.55);
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\node at (0,-0.75) {$50\text{ m}^{2}$};
\draw[<->] (0,1.55) -- (0,2.4);
\node[right] at (0.08,1.98) {$w$};
\node[below] at (0,-2.55) {total area $= 120\text{ m}^{2}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

